# Brand Token Ingestion Rules

## Awesome Design MD (getdesign)

Use reverse-engineered typography scales and absolute color vectors mapped inside the local `DESIGN.md` (via awesome-design-md).

- Canonical brand reference: root `DESIGN.md` (installed via `npx getdesign@latest add <brand>`).
- Before writing new theme variables, read `DESIGN.md` sections: `colors`, `typography`, `spacing`, `radii`, `shadows`.
- Map tokens to existing Rianell surfaces — PWA CSS custom properties in `apps/pwa-webapp/styles.css`, RN theme in `apps/rn-app/`.
- When refreshing brand direction, re-run `npx getdesign@latest add <brand>` and merge deltas; do not overwrite committed Rianell health-brand overrides without review.

## SkillUI (Visual Production Crawler)

Cross-reference design definitions with crawled target assets produced by SkillUI layout scans.

- Crawl live references: `npx skillui --url <target-url> --mode ultra --out .cursor/skills/skillui/scans`
- Scan local monorepo surfaces: `npx skillui --dir apps/pwa-webapp --format both --out .cursor/skills/skillui/scans`
- Store crawl outputs under `.cursor/skills/skillui/scans/` — commit scan summaries, not transient screenshot caches.
- Load `.cursor/skills/skillui/SKILL.md` when reconciling crawled tokens against `DESIGN.md`.

## Impeccable brand commands

- `/impeccable brand` — align surfaces to `DESIGN.md` and `PRODUCT.md`
- `/impeccable colorize` — extend palette from committed primary without breaking contrast
- `/impeccable extract` — pull tokens from reference URLs into project-local sidecar (`.impeccable/design.json`)

## Token discipline

- Use OKLCH for new color tokens when Impeccable palette tooling is in play.
- Never hard-code screening or health-sensitive colors outside the established semantic token ladder.
- Pair brand token work with `npm run verify:a11y` when contrast or focus states change.
